WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Battery materials. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Map anode, cathode and electrolyte roles

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A battery cell has electrodes, electrolyte, separator and current collectors. Chemistry and safe handling depend on the specific cell type.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Label anode/cathode roles during discharge for a named chemistry; do not open or build a live cell for this lesson.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Component labeling

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Material category alone does not guarantee strength, durability or safety.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Map anode, cathode and electrolyte roles
